1:# One-bar NQ stop scaling: Phases 2–4
3:Research status: **INCONCLUSIVE; EXPLORATORY; NOT APPROVED FOR LIVE**. The complete native-engine run and accounting checks finished. The result is a historical proxy-data experiment. It is not a verified MNQ execution result.
7:The experiment kept the promoted B0 entry and exit rules and added a protective stop at 1.5 times causal 20-bar ATR. The stop distance rounds up to the 0.25-point MNQ tick. Integer MNQ size is `floor($1,000 / ($2 × stop distance))`, based on the completed 30-minute bar available before entry. Each Chicago session remains capped at two filled entries. No B1 or B3 variants ran.
9:The source was the frozen one-minute Dukascopy USATECH.IDX/USD BID-only series, not dated CME futures. The simulation used the native ML4T Engine in annual isolated runs from 2013-01-01 through 2026-07-14 UTC, with $1,000,000 reset cash per year. The primary costed case used the frozen $1.25 commission and 0.25-point adverse slippage per MNQ contract per fill. The companion case used zero costs. Both cases used an illustrative $2,500 initial / $2,000 maintenance margin schedule.
15:CME specifies a $2-per-index-point MNQ multiplier and a 0.25-point tick worth $0.50. See [CME MNQ contract specifications](https://www.cmegroup.com/markets/equities/nasdaq/micro-e-mini-nasdaq-100.html) and the [CME micro equity index futures FAQ](https://www.cmegroup.com/articles/faqs/micro-e-mini-equity-index-futures-frequently-asked-questions.html). These contract terms do not make the underlying Dukascopy prices CME prices. Commission, slippage, and margin are illustrative assumptions; the BID-only source has no ASK or spread.
17:## Phase 3: causal event study
19:The fixed-entry B0 diagnostic found 5,150 closed trades with ATR20 context. It is an inference about B0 paths, not a B2 replay or a stop-parameter search. Median ATR20 / tick-rounded 1.5×ATR stop distances were 7.87 / 12.00 points in 2013–2017, 28.18 / 42.50 in 2018–2025, and 66.80 / 100.25 in 2026 through July 14. The corresponding diagnostic B0 path stop-touch counts were 104, 182, and 5. Same-minute events and changes to later entries mean these touches cannot be substituted for B2 fills.
23:| Case | Closed trades | Net P&L | Fees | Slippage | Entry contract sides | Actual stop exits |
25:| Zero cost | 5,459 | $308,023.53 | $0 | $0 | 128,702 | 306 |
28:The costed net result is the primary proxy outcome. Its gross P&L after slippage was $178,691.21. Net expectancy was −0.0254 R per trade; zero-cost expectancy was +0.0589 R. The large divergence makes cost assumptions and execution quality decisive. B0's historical costed result was +$166,107.92 over 5,462 trades, but B0 used one NQ contract and different commission units. This dollar comparison is not exposure-matched.
32:The run still has material limits. There were 64 costed same-minute entry/stop ambiguities because opposing STOP orders are not atomic OCO. Ninety-two scheduled market exits were late due to missing source points; the maximum delay was 2,976 minutes. Gap-through fills caused 138 costed trades to exceed $1,000 actual tick-rounded trigger risk; maximum observed risk was $1,584. Nominal sizing therefore does not cap realized loss. Costs and margin are not broker verified, and the source is not a CME feed. The 2026 period is observed stress data, not an unseen holdout.
36:The preregistered frozen specification remains SHA-256 `d38c96d7…f38f97e2`. During execution, an amendment added only the CME reference URLs after 2013–2016 had run. The supplement and time window are recorded in `frozen_spec_amendment.json`; no strategy, sizing, cost, date, or decision field changed. The amendment and timing reduce strict preregistration purity and are reported here.
38:Machine-readable source checks, event study, yearly fills/trades/equity, run ledger, native audit, final report, and hashes are under `run_log/one_bar_nq_stop_scaling_20261012/phase234/`. The runner and focused tests are `scripts/run_one_bar_nq_b2_20261012.py`, `scripts/run_one_bar_nq_b2_yearly_20261012.py`, and `tests/test_one_bar_nq_b2_20261012.py`. The protected promote tree and original session configuration were not edited. No commit, push, or live order was made.

