codex
The independent replay checks confirm why “all fills = two times closed trades” is too simple: the engine also records open positions and protective entry orders at year boundaries. I’m reconciling paired entry/exit fills against each closed trade, while separating those boundary orders. I also found 138 costed trades where a gap made realized stop risk exceed $1,000; the nominal sizing formula itself appears within budget, but I’m checking one floating point edge case before I finalize that conclusion.
