codex
The remaining discrepancy was a attribution bug in the verifier: an entry and its protective stop can both fill before the strategy callback, so the callback misses that entry. The old code then matched the trade to the nearest unrelated signal. I changed the reconciliation to use the native entry fill’s order ID and saved signal metadata. The 2024 replay now has no trade above $1,000 nominal trigger risk; I’m updating the full audit and preserving the failed intermediate attempt in the ledger.
